//    <name> THRESHOLD </name>
//    <rw> 
//    <i> [Bits 4..1] RW (@ 0x40000510) \nPower-fail comparator threshold setting. This setting applies both for normal voltage mode (supply connected to both VDD and VDDH) and high voltage mode (supply connected to VDDH only). Values 0-3 set threshold below 1.7 V and should not be used as brown out detection will be activated before power failure warning on such low voltages.\n0 : Reserved - do not use\n1 : Reserved - do not use\n2 : Reserved - do not use\n3 : Reserved - do not use\n4 : V17 = Set threshold to 1.7 V\n5 : V18 = Set threshold to 1.8 V\n6 : V19 = Set threshold to 1.9 V\n7 : V20 = Set threshold to 2.0 V\n8 : V21 = Set threshold to 2.1 V\n9 : V22 = Set threshold to 2.2 V\n10 : V23 = Set threshold to 2.3 V\n11 : V24 = Set threshold to 2.4 V\n12 : V25 = Set threshold to 2.5 V\n13 : V26 = Set threshold to 2.6 V\n14 : V27 = Set threshold to 2.7 V\n15 : V28 = Set threshold to 2.8 V </i>
//    <combo> 
//      <loc> ( (unsigned int) POWER_POFCON ) </loc>
//      <o.4..1> THRESHOLD
//        <0=> 0: 
